{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793640378,"nonce":"TsdKAjo3xDj9R0tTuas8uF8L0vk=","title":"Canvas path batches dispatch at a sample count of 1, so paths are never antialiased","message":"The app is configured with sample_count 4 (\"4x MSAA for path anti-aliasing\", blinc_app/src/app.rs), and frame_dispatch.rs still passes self.sample_count to render_paths_overlay_msaa. The ordered and foreground canvas batches added by bfa48788 and 5e444d7a, and the overlay foreground path, call render_overlay_msaa(.., 1): context/canvas_order.rs (both dispatch functions) and context/overlay_rendering.rs. A canvas's fill_path/stroke_path output therefore renders aliased on desktop: stair-stepped curves and rounded corners. The path shader's own edge AA is disabled (note in path.wgsl). dd6a0d6's tests cover ordered batches at 4x, so passing the configured count looks safe; nothing recorded explains the 1.\n\ncn charts no longer depend on this (they draw SDF primitives and capsules). Wanted: pass self.sample_count at those sites, with a GPU test that a curved canvas path through the ordered dispatch has blended edge pixels at 4x.","files":null}]}